New York.—The steamship Olympics dispatch follows;

"Carpathia reached Titanic position at daybreak. Found boats and wreckage only. Titanic sank about 2:20 a. m. in 41:16 N. 50:14 W. All her boats accounted for, containing about 675 souls saved, crew and passengers included. Nearly all saved are women and children. Leyland liner Californian remained and searched exact position of disaster. Loss likely 800 souls"

It is believed here that this is an error—unless the Titanic had more passengers on board that reported. The list as given out showed 1910 passengers and a crew of 560 or 570 persons in all. Deducting 675, the known saved, would indicate a loss of 1,800 persons.

